lv9hx157/13cc52c7-48d3-4314-9624-38c437422fc9/7254a4c0-ffd9-11ee-a65d-61c1e650eee9/file-1lv9hx158.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1lv9hx157/13cc52c7-48d3-4314-9624-38c437422fc9/7254a4c0-ffd9-11ee-a65d-61c1e650eee9/file-1lv9hx158.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1lv9hx157/13cc52c7-48d3-4314-9624-38c437422fc9/7254a4c0-ffd9-11ee-a65d-61c1e650eee9/file-1lv9hx158.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1lv9hx157/13cc52c7-48d3-4314-9624-38c437422fc9/7254a4c0-ffd9-11ee-a65d-61c1e650eee9/file-1lv9hx158.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"4 : 1"},{"identifier":"B","content":"2 : 1"},{"identifier":"C","content":"1 : 2"},{"identifier":"D","content":"1 : 1"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<p>To determine the ratio of heat dissipated per second through resistances <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.765ex\" height=\"1.643ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -704 1222 726\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"3A9\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3A9\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.896ex\" height=\"1.643ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -704 1722 726\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"><use data-c=\"3A9\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3A9\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> in the given parallel circuit, let's break it down step by step.</p>\n\n<p><b>Understanding the Problem</b></p>\n\n<p>When resistors are connected in parallel:</p>\n\n<ol>\n\n<li>The voltage across each resistor is the same.</li><br>\n\n<li>The power dissipated in each resistor can be found using the formula:</li>\n\n</ol>\n\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.814ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"7.735ex\" height=\"3.04ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -983.7 3418.9 1343.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1028.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(2084.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D449\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D449\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(861.3,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(398.8,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D445\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D445\"></use></g><rect width=\"1094.4\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n\n<p><b>Applying the Power Formula in Parallel Resistors</b></p>\n\n<p>Given:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\n<li><mjx-container c